==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Idi:N2''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Idi:NX''' after beating [[The Face of God/Invasion|The Face of God Invasion]] and using [[Behemoth Stone|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Idi:N2 is a short-ranged rusher similar to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]]. Her high damage against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] (exceeding 230,000 at level 40 per hit and 280,000 at level 50), curse immunity and fast movement speed make her ideal for [[Loris]] in particular, infiltrating his blind spot to quickly take him out. Shorter-ranged relics like Sir Rel, Relic Doge, [[Mr. Puffington|Puffington]] and even Oldhorn are also no match for her when properly supported, as well as those with a somewhat significant attack frequency, namely Dogumaru and Othom. Just be wary of her health, as most Relic enemies tend to deal very high damage. In this aspect, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]] can be very useful as he could freeze Relic enemies for several seconds, buying Idi enough time to inflict 2 particularly lethal hits.

Her immunity to [[Surge Attack]]s is mostly useful for the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]], [[Esoteric Uril (Enemy)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]], [[Evil Emperor Cat]], [[:Category:Death Surge Enemies|Death Surge enemies]] and maybe [[Raynard]] or [[Red EnerG]], as other [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge Attackers]] like [[Kappy Jr.]], [[St. Dober]] and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]] would easily kill her with their normal attacks before she does anything relevant.

This unit is very well worth doing {{4c}} Stories of Legend for, and it shows even more in her True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Idi:NX's most notable improvement is the Insane Damage ability, which greatly increases her damage against Relics. At level 42, she can kill a 100% [[Mr. Puffington]] in one hit, a 100% [[Othom]] in two, and later at level 48 a 100% [[M. Ost]] in three. Her matchup against [[Lowkey]] gets even better with the health boost. Being obtainable after 1-Crown UL, she is able to demolish even the buffed Relics of 2/3-Crown UL. Sage Slayer and Immune to [[Explosion]]s are fairly niche, being primarily useful against [[Revival of Origin/Invasion|Revival of Origin Invasion]]'s main threat, [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]] and [[Shachiko]]. Both are Relic [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]] that inflict high damage at range with Nova wielding devastating Explosions, though Idi can quickly decimate them by entering their blindspots. Her health increase doesn't matter too much as she's still quite frail, but the extra health does allow her to take an extra hit from some enemies, especially Sages.

Overall, this [[True Form]] is well worth the Yellow Behemoth Gems and Epic Behemoth Stones.

